  <sys:String x:Key="Target.DnsServer">DNS server</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Target.HostHint">After prep, QRP sync uses the hub service account (no more manual registry edits).</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Target.CredsBody">DNS server administrator (or Domain Admin) for WinRM. Recommended format: DOMAIN\user.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Target.Account">Account</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Target.Password">Password</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Target.PersistCreds">Remember account (DPAPI LocalMachine under ProgramData\DnsBlocker\secrets)</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Target.CredsHint">The password is never written to logs. One-shot transfer over the local named pipe to the service.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Target.TestBody">Test WinRM/CIM, then choose remote prep options.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Target.HubIdentity">Hub identity to authorize (empty = auto: DnsBlocker service account or DnsAdmins)</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Target.AddDnsAdmins">Also add this identity to the DnsAdmins group (AD risk — documented)</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Target.ApplyBody">Remote steps: DNS Server registry ACL (Full Control) → Add/Remove QRP probe. Click Prepare.</sys:String>
